## One addition, this wave (integrator; inside UIR-04's write scope)

`DemoGateAdapter.badge_text_key_for(build_id)` — `js/ui.js:744` selects the badge by the
build's own name (`betaBadge` for a beta, `demoBadge` for a demo), a question
`badge_text_key()` could not answer because the port reaches only `demo`/`full`
(`BuildFlag.is_demo()`). The function is additive: `badge_text_key()` is byte-identical in
behaviour, and the two new constants (`BADGE_DEMO_KEY`, `BADGE_BETA_KEY`) name the strings
the reference itself uses. UIR-07's capture states call it; UIR-23 still owns the beta
build label, and the port's frozen locale table has no `betaBadge` entry (recorded in
`uir-07-screen-menu.log`).
